  "contract": [
    "Write only push.autoSetupRemote=true and push.default=simple to the selected local repository configuration. Preserve other local values and global/system configuration.",
    "Verify readback and preserve original caller-specific validation, warning and failure-code behavior.",
    "Return a native PowerShell Hashtable with Success, Errors and Values without exiting or throwing from configuration failures. Preserve LASTEXITCODE, including a prior or undefined value when no Git process ran.",
    "Retain missing-tool and malformed-child-response failure tables; a bad protocol cannot become success.",
    "Git configuration uses its native lock. Never delete another writer config.lock. A second-write failure can leave the first key updated; this is not a transaction across keys.",
    "Git subprocesses have 30-second deadlines and report failure visibly."
  ],
  "profile_boundaries": {
    "bash": "Git itself checks the root; readback comparison is case sensitive; Git-version failure and write failures preserve their native exit codes.",
    "powershell": "Require an existing directory; readback comparison is case insensitive; malformed or failed Git-version probes remain best effort. Native formatting, Hashtable and LASTEXITCODE adaptation remain PowerShell."
  },
  "red_green": {
    "native_prior_exit_state": "Two native missing-directory/file cases failed before preserving the scalar prior value, because a saved PSVariable object changed with LASTEXITCODE. All 17 native profile controls then passed."
  },
  "host_limits": [
    "Local evidence is Linux, PowerShell 7.5.3 and CPython 3.14.10. A separate Windows PowerShell 5.1 control is registered for Windows CI and cannot execute on Linux.",
    "POSIX executable Git shims and Bash compatibility controls are explicitly host limited; the portable policy corpus and real native PowerShell profiles run separately.",
    "uv is a prerequisite. Missing uv produces a native failure table without exiting the caller.",
    "The read-only healthy push gate does not call this repair/configuration path. Bootstrap and explicit repair callers are affected by retained CLI startup regressions."
  ],
